Guidance NEWS
=============

0.2.0 (2026-11-22), an alpha release
------------------------------------

The first release that works as a debugger.

* Running programs.  Guidance takes a subset of Guile's command line
  (-L, -C, -l, -s, -c, -e, -x, --use-srfi, --fresh-auto-compile) and
  runs the program as `guile` would, with its own command line.  Open
  Program (Ctrl+O) chooses another.  Guile's --debug, --no-debug,
  --auto-compile, --no-auto-compile and -q are accepted and ignored.

* Pausing.  Breakpoints at lines (from the Source page, F9, or a click
  in its margin) and at procedures (from the Modules page, or with
  add-trap-at-procedure-call! in the REPL) last from run to run.
  `_break_` pauses at the line that calls it; Pause (F6) pauses a
  running program.  Programs are compiled with some optimizations off,
  so that variables keep their names.

* Stepping.  Step Over (F10), Step Into (F11) and Step Out
  (Shift+F11) go by line, and two more buttons go by expression.
  Stepping skips Guile's own libraries.

* Inspecting.  In Error and Trap mode, the Backtrace page shows the
  program's stack and the arguments and local variables of each frame,
  and expressions are evaluated in the selected frame.  `_pk_` logs
  values on the Peek page.

* The Terminal shows output and error output in the order they were
  written, in a monospace font, takes multi-line expressions, keeps a
  history (Up, Down, and a menu), and sends end-of-file with Ctrl+D.
  Guile's notes about compiling are hidden.

* Safety.  Errors in a program's other threads are reported without
  disturbing Guidance, and recursion without end stops at a 256 MiB
  stack with the stack shown.

* The Threads page lists the program's threads; the Source page has
  line numbers and marks breakpoints.  Guidance caches its own
  compiled Scheme modules, so it starts in well under a second after
  the first time.

* Tests: a REPL test of the debugger core in plain Guile, and a GUI
  test on Xvfb, run by `meson test` and by GitHub Actions, with and
  without the address and undefined-behavior sanitizers.

0.1.0 (2021-12-09)
------------------

An early prototype.
